    '|a||And the raise is the same five thousand, every year for forty years. Spending rises by the full five thousand.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:120xxyp'
    '|b||And that cracks Kuznets''s puzzle. As a country grows richer, permanent income grows too, and spending keeps pace, so the share saved needn''t climb.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Friedman''s smoothing runs on a paycheck that never stops. In 1954 Franco Modigliani and his student Richard Brumberg built in the obvious catch: one day it does.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11560
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Say Jonas works from thirty, retires at seventy and lives to eighty. Ten years with no paycheck.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1p48ooz'
    '|a||Forty years of earnings now have to last fifty years, so he spends forty thousand a year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1f0t84s'
    '|b||And the gap while he works is saving, which he lives off once he stops.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1fweiuh'
    '|a||So his savings climb to a peak at retirement, then run down. Modigliani called it the life cycle.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:sdl0eb'
    '|b||Then the raise must look different now too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1x7xrmx'
    '|b||With retirement in the picture, how much of a $5,000 raise does Jonas spend each year? Click on the line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:5p5o81'
    '|a||Four thousand: forty years of raises, spread over fifty years of life. The other thousand goes towards retirement.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||And the bonus shrinks to a hundred dollars a year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:kbq958'
    '|a||Same core as Friedman: spending follows lifetime resources, not this year''s pay. The two differed on the horizon.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1mqowb0'
    '|b||Modigliani meant a whole life. Friedman himself thought people looked only about three years ahead, and would spend about a third of a windfall in its first year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:maqoqi'
    '|a||Modigliani drew a bold conclusion for whole countries: their saving depends less on how rich they are than on how fast they grow and how old they are.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:uu54re'
    '|b||Because workers save and retirees spend down. A young, fast-growing country has more savers than spenders.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ml1yps'
    '|a||The arithmetic behind those numbers is short. Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:16amor'
    '|a||With no interest, Jonas spends his lifetime earnings divided by his years of life: forty years of fifty thousand, over fifty years, is forty thousand.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11120
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Any extra pay adds its size, times the years it lasts, divided by the years of life.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:m23s2b'
    '|a||A bonus lasts one year: five thousand over fifty, a hundred dollars.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1c6yw3o'
    '|a||A raise lasts forty: four thousand a year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:bhdepy'
    '|a||The life cycle has old people running their savings down to nothing. Do they?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||My grandmother didn''t. She died in her own house, with money in the bank.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1j8mu0h'
    '|a||She''s typical. Many people run their wealth down far more slowly than the model says: some keep a cushion for illness or care, many want to leave something behind.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:nhlk7v'
    '|a||In 1981 Laurence Kotlikoff and Lawrence Summers put a number on it: roughly four-fifths of American wealth, they estimated, came from inheritances and gifts, not from saving for retirement.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1a0z0nq'
    '|b||Modigliani pushed back hard: by his count, closer to a fifth.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:l5s79a'
    '|a||Much of the gap is definitions: does the interest on an inheritance count as inherited, or the college fees your parents paid?':
